      "plankton_bloom": "Plankton Bloom",
      "plankton_blooms_occur_when_nutrients_o": "Plankton blooms occur when nutrients (often from upwelling or runoff) spike. They feed the entire pelagic food web — phytoplankton → krill → small fish → cephalopods → top predators. Massive blooms can become harmful (HABs) when toxic dinoflagellates dominate.",
      "planned_additions_to_the_simulator_202": "Planned additions to the simulator (2026+):\n\n• Multiplayer mode (students collaborate on simulator missions)\n• Voice-over for accessibility\n• Languages other than English (Spanish, Portuguese, Mandarin priority)\n• Local-content authoring (teachers add their own scenarios)\n• Integration with iNaturalist + REEF citizen-science workflows\n• Better progress tracking + portfolio export\n• AI-assisted comprehension checking\n• More cephalopod species (especially deep-sea + cold-water species)\n• Better mobile / tablet support\n\nIf you're a developer or designer + want to contribute, please reach out.",
