      "hot_work_permits_are_required_in_many_": "Hot work permits are required in many industrial settings. Sweep area before welding (especially flammable debris). Have ABC fire extinguisher within 35 ft. Hot work watch (someone else watching for fire) for 30 min minimum after stopping. Most shop fires start hours after welding from smoldering material — not during welding itself.",
      "hot_work_without_a_fire_watch": "Hot Work Without a Fire Watch",
      "hours_to_days_after_welding_often_call": "Hours to DAYS after welding. Often called \"delayed cracking\" because it appears overnight or even later.",
      "how_deep_into_the_base_metal_the_fusio": " — how deep into the base metal the fusion actually went.",
      "how_et_works": "🔧 How ET works",
      "how_it_works": "🔧 How it works",
      "how_robotic_welding_gets_programmed": "⌨ How robotic welding gets programmed",
      "how_safe_is_your_shop": "🛡 How safe is your shop?",
      "how_to_become_cwi": "🎓 How to become CWI",
      "how_to_get_in": "How to get in",
